     "page": 1,
     "text": "Garcia-Davis Medical Group\nRe: Alexis Gardner (DOB 10/15/1955)\n\nDear Life Insurer,\n\nI am writing to provide you with a comprehensive medical summary of Mrs. Alexis Gardner, who has been under my care at Garcia-Davis Medical Group. Below, you will find detailed information regarding her medical conditions, treatments, and overall health status as of her last visit on January 10, 2025.\n\nOn January 10, 2025, Mrs. Gardner was seen for concerning her PVCs (Premature Ventricular Contractions), SVT (Supraventricular Tachycardia), WPW (Wolff-Parkinson-White) syndrome, BBB (Bundle Branch Block), pacemaker, and syncope. Her blood pressure at this visit was 122/76, and her weight was recorded at 115 pounds. Mrs. Gardner is currently doing well with her pacemaker, which was ablated, and her condition remains controlled.\n\nOn April 16, 2024, Gardner visited the clinic for a back strain. Her blood pressure was 1Z8/67, and she weighed 121 pounds at the time. This visit also provided an opportunity to review her known conditions, including her PVCs, SVT, WPW syndrome, BBB, pacemaker, and syncope, all of which have been managed effectively. Additionally, she has been diagnosed with asthma, which is controlled with albuterol 90 mcg inhaler. She has had three steroid bursts per year and an visit 7.7 years ago. Currently, she is on biologic therapy for her asthma.\n\nIn July 2023, Mrs. Gardner visited the clinic for gout. Her blood pressure was 134/76, and she weighed 119 pounds. During this visit, we again reviewed her PVCs, SVT, WPW syndrome, BBB, pacemaker, and syncope, all of which continue to be well-managed. Her gout is also controlled, and she is on allopurinol 300 mg daily. \n\nMrs. Gardner was seen again on October 24, 2022, for her PVCs, SVT, WPW syndrome, BBB, pacemaker, and syncope. Her blood pressure at that visit was 125/68, and she weighed 112 pounds. Her condition remained stable, and she was doing well.\n\nOn January 27, 2022, Mrs. Gardner visited the clinic for gout. Her blood pressure was 127/76, and her weight was 122 pounds. At this visit, her gout was well-controlled, and her other conditions were also stable.\n\nSocial reveals that Mrs. Gardner used to smoke cigarettes, with a frequency of 10 per day, but she quit on June 3, 2017. She has been honest about her tobacco use history.\n\nAdditionally, it is worth noting that Mrs. Gardner has been diagnosed with glaucoma since July 29, 2024, which is currently controlled with timolol ophthalmic 0.5% eye drops.\n\nPlease let me know if you require any further information additional details.\n"
